Restricted Entities Clause

This clause is an additional condition on the permission granted above. Where
it and the MIT text disagree, this clause narrows who may use the Software; it
does not widen anything. Because of it, this project is source-available rather
than OSI-approved open source.

This software and its derivatives may not be used by, or on behalf of, the
following entities:

- Government Bodies: any state, regional, or local government agency,
  ministry, or administrative department.
- Military & Intelligence: any armed forces, intelligence agencies, or law
  enforcement organizations.
- State-Owned Enterprises: any corporation, company, or entity where a
  government holds a controlling stake or majority ownership.
- Political Organizations: any political party, political action committee, or
  entity actively engaged in political campaigning or lobbying.
- Defense Contractors: any private entity using this software directly for the
  fulfillment of military, defense, or state security contracts.

Individual people, private businesses, and non-governmental organizations are
not affected by this clause.
